  "description": "The \u0027cluster_tasks_by_projectKey\u0027 dataset is designed to provide insights into task management and scheduling across various projects. Each entry in the dataset represents a unique project identified by the \u0027projectKey\u0027. The dataset includes temporal metrics such as the earliest and latest start times (\u0027start_time_min\u0027 and \u0027start_time_max\u0027), which help in understanding the scheduling and execution timeline of tasks within a project. Additionally, it provides duration metrics, including the maximum and average duration of tasks in seconds (\u0027duration_seconds_max\u0027 and \u0027duration_seconds_avg\u0027), offering insights into task efficiency and time management. The dataset also tracks the age of tasks in days, from minimum to maximum (\u0027age_days_min\u0027 and \u0027age_days_max\u0027), which can be useful for analyzing task lifecycle and project timelines. The \u0027count\u0027 column indicates the number of tasks associated with each project, providing a measure of project activity. This dataset is valuable for project managers and analysts looking to optimize task scheduling, improve time management, and gain a comprehensive view of project timelines and task durations.",
  "shortDesc": "Project task clustering dataset with time and duration metrics.",
